  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "If five geometric means are inserted between \\(8\\) and \\(5832,\\) the fifth term in the geometric series is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(648\\)",
    "B": "\\(832\\)",
    "C": "\\(1168\\)",
    "D": "\\(1944\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Five inserted means, together with the two endpoints, give seven terms. Let \\(q\\ne0\\) be the real common ratio. Going from the first term \\(8\\) to the seventh term \\(5832\\) requires six multiplications by \\(q\\), so\n\\[\n8q^6=5832,\n\\qquad q^6=729=3^6.\n\\]\nThus \\(q=3\\) or \\(q=-3\\); if all inserted means are required to be positive, only \\(q=3\\) is used. The fifth term is four steps after the first, and either real ratio gives\n\\[\na_5=8q^4=8\\cdot81=648.\n\\]\nTherefore the fifth term is \\(\\boxed{648}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
